cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "trialplate: Sample-Size Diagnostics for Data-Driven Trial Eligibility Criteria"
abstract: >-
  Rules that relax clinical-trial eligibility criteria from real-world data make two
  separate promises: more eligible patients, and no loss in the estimated treatment
  effect. trialplate validates both out of sample and supplies diagnostics that are
  computable before any outcome is examined, including a closed-form interaction
  leverage and a detector for criteria that logically imply one another.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Runshu
    family-names: Wang
    email: runshu.wang@gmail.com
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-30"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/USER/trialplate"
keywords:
  - eligibility criteria
  - trial emulation
  - real-world data
  - Shapley value
  - non-collapsibility
  - restricted mean survival time
  - out-of-sample validation
